---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import About from "../components/About.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---
<Base
  title="ve"
  description="Viscoelastic earthquake cycles from boundary elements alone: postseismic motion, the cycle of a locked fault, afterslip and a subducting slab, with no volume mesh."
  current="home"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    <h1>ve<span class="sub">viscoelastic earthquake cycles, boundary elements only</span></h1>
    <About />
  </Fragment>

  <div
    id="hero"
    class="hero"
    aria-label="A block diagram of a megathrust cut at mid-strike: the free surface and the cut face through the plate and the mantle, coloured by how far each point has moved vertically since the earthquake and displaced by that motion, looping from the earthquake to one hundred relaxation times"
  ></div>
  <p class="cap">
    A megathrust cut at mid-strike, from the earthquake to 100 Maxwell times
    after it. Colour is the <b>vertical displacement since the earthquake</b>
    (red up, blue down), on the free surface and on the cut face, and both are
    displaced by the motion itself, exaggerated. The fault (<b>pink</b>) dips
    20&deg; through a 30&nbsp;km elastic plate into a Maxwell substrate; the
    rupture is 300&nbsp;km long and the face is 180&nbsp;km deep. Nothing
    inside the block was meshed: the model's 219,315 unknowns are all on
    boundaries, it was solved fourteen times, once per Laplace state, and the
    field on the cut face is read from the boundaries. Drag to orbit. See
    <a href={`${base}concepts/`}>Concepts</a> for how fourteen elastic solves
    become every time, and <a href={`${base}examples/`}>Examples</a> to move
    the clock yourself.
  </p>

  <style>
    .hero { position: relative; min-height: 440px; width: 100%; overflow: hidden; cursor: grab; }
    .hero:active { cursor: grabbing; }
  </style>
  <style is:global>
    .hero canvas { display: block; }
    .hero .clock {
      position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 4px; font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--fg-dim); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      pointer-events: none;
    }
  </style>
  <script>
    import { startHero } from "../viz/hero";
    startHero(document.getElementById("hero")!, import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
  </script>
</Base>
